'''York Central''' is a parliamentary [[United Kingdom constituencies|constituency]]{{#tag:ref|A [[borough constituency]] (for the purposes of election expenses and type of returning officer)|group= n}} which is represented in the [[House of Commons of the United Kingdom|House of Commons]] of the [[UK Parliament]] by [[Rachael Maskell]] of the [[Labour Party (UK)|Labour Party]] and the [[Co-operative Party]].{{#tag:ref|As with all constituencies, the constituency elects one [[Member of Parliament (United Kingdom)|Member of Parliament]] (MP) by the [[first past the post]] system of election at least every five years.|group= n}}

==Constituency profile==
The seat covers the historic centre of York which is a significant tourist destination, and surrounding suburbs including Acomb, Clifton and Fishergate. Residents' health and wealth are slightly above the UK averages.<ref>Electoral Calculus https://www.electoralcalculus.co.uk/fcgi-bin/seatdetails.py?seat=York+Central</ref>

==Creation==
After the [[2005 United Kingdom general election|2005 general election]] the parliamentary representation in [[North Yorkshire]] was reviewed by the [[Boundary Commission for England]], which recommended the division of the former [[City of York (UK Parliament constituency)|City of York constituency]] before the [[2010 United Kingdom general election|2010 general election]] leading to two constituencies within the borders of the city of [[York]] - '''York Central''' is entirely surrounded by [[York Outer]].

York Central is one of only two UK Parliament constituencies to be surrounded by another constituency. The other constituency, [[Bath (UK Parliament constituency)|Bath]], is entirely surrounded by [[North East Somerset]].

==Boundaries==
{{maplink|raw={{Wikipedia:Map data/York Central (UK Parliament constituency) 2010}}|frame=yes|frame-align=right|text=Map of 2010-2024 boundaries}}

'''2010–2024''': The city of York wards of: [[Acomb, North Yorkshire|Acomb]]; [[Clifton, York|Clifton]]; [[Fishergate]]; [[York Guildhall|Guildhall]]; [[Heworth, York|Heworth]]; [[Holgate, North Yorkshire|Holgate]]; Hull Road; [[Micklegate]]; and Westfield.

'''2024–present''': Same as before but with changed ward boundaries.

