'''Normanton and Hemsworth''' is a [[List of UK Parliament constituencies|constituency]] of the [[House of Commons of the United Kingdom|House of Commons]] in the [[Parliament of the United Kingdom|UK Parliament]]. The constituency was created by the [[2023 Periodic Review of Westminster constituencies]], and will first be contested at the [[2024 United Kingdom general election|2024 general election]] on 4 July.<ref>{{cite web |title=Yorkshire and the Humber {{!}} Boundary Commission for England |url=https://boundarycommissionforengland.independent.gov.uk/2023-review/yorkshire-and-the-humber/ |access-date=20 June 2023 |website=[[Boundary Commission for England]]}}</ref>

== History ==
The constituency was formed primarily from the existing [[Hemsworth (UK Parliament constituency)|Hemsworth]] constituency - excluding the Wakefield South ward, with the addition of [[Normanton, West Yorkshire|Normanton]] from [[Normanton, Pontefract and Castleford (UK Parliament constituency)|Normanton, Pontefract and Castleford]] (renamed [[Pontefract, Castleford and Knottingley (UK Parliament constituency)|Pontefract, Castleford and Knottingley]]).<ref>{{cite web |last=Gittins |first=Holly |date=8 June 2021 |title=Boundary Commission proposals: Major shakeup of parliamentary constituencies in Wakefield, Pontefract and Castleford could see borders moved and new constituency created |url=https://www.wakefieldexpress.co.uk/news/politics/boundary-commission-proposals-major-shakeup-of-parliamentary-constituencies-in-wakefield-pontefract-and-castleford-could-see-borders-moved-and-new-constituency-created-3265119 |website=Wakefield Express|accessdate=5 August 2023}}</ref>

== Boundaries ==
The constituency comprised the following wards of the [[City of Wakefield]] (as they existed on 1 December 2020):<ref>{{cite web |title=New Seat Details - Normanton and Hemsworth |url=https://www.electoralcalculus.co.uk/fcgi-bin/calcwork23.py?seat=Normanton%20and%20Hemsworth |access-date=5 August 2023 |website=[[Electoral Calculus]]}}</ref>

* [[Ackworth, West Yorkshire|Ackworth]], [[North Elmsall]] and [[Upton, West Yorkshire|Upton]]
* [[Crofton, West Yorkshire|Crofton]], [[Ryhill]] and [[Walton, Wakefield|Walton]]
* [[Featherstone]]
* [[Hemsworth]]
* [[Normanton, West Yorkshire|Normanton]]
* [[South Elmsall]] and [[South Kirkby]]<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |title=The Parliamentary Constituencies Order 2023 |url=https://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2023/1230/schedules/made |at=Schedule 1 Part 9 Yorkshire and the Humber region}}</ref>

