'''Brigg and Immingham''' is a [[List of UK Parliament constituencies|constituency]] of the [[House of Commons of the United Kingdom|House of Commons]] in the [[Parliament of the United Kingdom|UK Parliament]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Yorkshire and the Humber {{!}} Boundary Commission for England |url=https://boundarycommissionforengland.independent.gov.uk/2023-review/yorkshire-and-the-humber/ |access-date=20 June 2023 |website=[[Boundary Commission for England]]}}</ref> Created as a result of the [[2023 Periodic Review of Westminster constituencies]], it will first be contested at the [[2024 United Kingdom general election|2024 general election]].<ref>{{Cite news |date=2022-11-08 |title=Latest boundary plans stick to Grimsby and Cleethorpes merger |url=https://www.grimsbytelegraph.co.uk/news/local-news/latest-boundary-plans-stick-controversial-7796961 |access-date=2024-03-07 |work=Grimsby Live |language=en-GB |issn=0307-1235}}</ref>

== Boundaries ==
Following a local government boundary review in North Lincolnshire which came into effect in May 2023,<ref>{{Cite web |last=LGBCE |title=North Lincolnshire {{!}} LGBCE |url=https://www.lgbce.org.uk/all-reviews/north-lincolnshire |access-date=2024-04-14 |website=www.lgbce.org.uk |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=The North Lincolnshire (Electoral Changes) Order 2022 |url=https://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2022/1139/contents/made}}</ref> the constituency comprises the following from the 2024 general election:

*The Borough of North East Lincolnshire wards of: Humberston and New Waltham; Immingham; Scartho; Waltham; Wolds.
*The District of North Lincolnshire wards of: Barton; Brigg & Wolds (majority; all parts except Cadney and Howsham); Broughton & Scawby (majority; all parts except Scawby and Scawby Brook); Burton upon Stather & Winterton (small part covering Appleby, Dragonby, Roxby and Santon); Ferry.<ref>{{Cite web |title=The Parliamentary Constituencies Order 2023 |url=https://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2023/1230/schedules/made |at=Schedule 1 Part 9 Yorkshire and the Humber region}}</ref> 

It comprises the following:<ref>{{Cite web |title=New Seat Details - Brigg and Immingham |url=https://www.electoralcalculus.co.uk/fcgi-bin/calcwork23.py?seat=Brigg+and+Immingham |access-date=2024-03-07 |website=www.electoralcalculus.co.uk}}</ref>
* The majority of the abolished [[Cleethorpes (UK Parliament constituency)|Cleethorpes]] constituency - excluding the town of [[Cleethorpes]] itself (included in the new constituency of [[Great Grimsby and Cleethorpes (UK Parliament constituency)|Great Grimsby and Cleethorpes]])
* The [[Scartho]] ward from the abolished [[Great Grimsby (UK Parliament constituency)|Great Grimsby]] constituency
* The  towns of [[Brigg]] and [[Broughton, Lincolnshire|Broughton]], and rural areas to the north, from the abolished [[Brigg and Goole (UK Parliament constituency)|Brigg and Goole]] constituency.

