t and Pudsey |url=https://westleedsdispatch.com/boundary-commission-publishes-final-boundary-changes-heres-what-it-means-for-people-living-in-leeds-west-and-pudsey/ |access-date=2024-03-06 |website=West Leeds Dispatch |language=en-GB}}</ref>
== Boundaries == The constituency is composed of the following (as they existed on 1 December 2020):
* The City of Leeds wards of: Headingley & Hyde Park; Kirkstall; Little London & Woodhouse; Weetwood.<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |title=The Parliamentary Constituencies Order 2023 |url=https://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2023/1230/schedules/made |at=Schedule 1 Part 9 Yorkshire and the Humber region}}</ref>
It comprises the following areas of the [[City of Leeds]]:<ref>{{Cite web |title=New Seat Details - Leeds Central and Headingley |url=https://www.electoralcalculus.co.uk/fcgi-bin/calcwork23.py?seat=Leeds+Central+and+Headingley |access-date=2024-03-06 |website=www.electoralcalculus.co.uk}}</ref> * [[Headingley]] and [[Weetwood]], transferred from [[Leeds North West (UK Parliament constituency)|Leeds North West]] * [[Hyde Park, Leeds|Hyde Park]], [[Little London, Leeds|Little London]] and [[Woodhouse, Leeds|Woodhouse]] from [[Leeds Central (UK Parliament constituency)|Leeds Central]] (to be abolished and largely replaced by [[Leeds South (UK Parliament constituency)|Leeds South]]) * [[Kirkstall]] from [[Leeds West (UK Parliament constituency)|Leeds West]] (to be abolished)
