Another general election was required to take place before the end of 1940. The political parties had been making preparations for an election to take place from 1939 and by the end of this year, the following candidates had been selected: *'''Labour'''; [[Hastings Lees-Smith]] *'''Conservative'''; Gay Burdett <ref>Yorkshire Post and Leeds Intelligencer 24 August 1939</ref>
