{{Short description|Parliamentary constituency in the United Kingdom, 2024 onwards}} {{Use dmy dates|date=December 2023}} {{Infobox UK constituency main |name = Dewsbury and Batley |parliament = uk |image = {{maplink|frame=yes|frame-align=center|plain=yes|raw={{Wikipedia:Map data/Dewsbury and Batley (UK Parliament constituency)}}|frame-height=200|frame-width=250}} |caption = Boundaries since 2024 |image2 = [[File:Yorkshire and the Humber - Dewsbury and Batley constituency.svg|215px|alt=Map of constituency]] |caption2 = Boundary of Dewsbury and Batley in Yorkshire and the Humber |year = 2024 |abolished = |type = Borough |previous = {{ubl|[[Dewsbury (UK Parliament constituency)|Dewsbury]] (majority)|[[Batley and Spen (UK Parliament constituency)|Batley and Spen]] (minority)}} |next = |electorate = |mp = [[Iqbal Mohamed]] |party = [[Labour Party (UK)|Labour]] |region = England |county = [[West Yorkshire]] |elects_howmany = One |towns = {{ubl|[[Batley]]|[[Dewsbury]]|[[Kirkburton]]|[[Thornhill, West Yorkshire|Thornhill]]}} }} '''Dewsbury and Batley''' is a [[List of UK Parliament constituencies|constituency]] of the [[House of Commons of the United Kingdom|House of Commons]] in the [[Parliament of the United Kingdom|UK Parliament]].<ref>{{cite web |title=The 2023 Review of Parliamentary Constituency Boundaries in England – Volume one: Report – Yorkshire and the Humber {{!}} Boundary Commission for England |url=https://boundarycommissionforengland.independent.gov.uk/2023-review/2023-review-volume-one-report/the-2023-review-of-parliamentary-constituency-boundaries-in-england-volume-one-report-yorkshire-and-the-humber/ |access-date=25 July 2023 |website=boundarycommissionforengland.independent.gov.uk}}</ref> Further to the completion of the [[2023 Periodic Review of Westminster constituencies]], it will first be contested in the [[2024 United Kingdom general election|2024 general election]].<ref>{{Cite news |date=2023-05-18 |title=Batley and Spen MP ignores safe seat advice as constituency is split |language=en-GB |work=BBC News |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/uk-england-leeds-65625851 |access-date=2023-12-02}}</ref> The constituency is located in the borough of [[Kirklees]] in [[West Yorkshire]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Marlow |first=Abigail |date=2022-11-10 |title=Kim Leadbeater slams new Kirklees boundaries that will split up Batley |url=https://www.examinerlive.co.uk/news/local-news/kim-leadbeater-slams-new-kirklees-25476708 |access-date=2023-12-02 |website=Yorkshire Live |language=en}}</ref>
== Boundaries == The constituency composed of the following (as they existed on 1 December 2020):
* The Borough of Kirklees wards of Batley East; Batley West; Dewsbury East; Dewsbury South; Dewsbury West; Kirkburton (polling districts KB04, KB07A, KB07B and KB10).<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |title=The Parliamentary Constituencies Order 2023 |url=https://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2023/1230/schedules/made |at=Schedule 1 Part 9 Yorkshire and the Humber region}}</ref>
It comprises the following areas of [[Kirklees]]:<ref>{{Cite web |title=New Seat Details - Dewsbury and Batley |url=https://www.electoralcalculus.co.uk/fcgi-bin/calcwork23.py?seat=Dewsbury%20and%20Batley |access-date=2023-12-02 |website=www.electoralcalculus.co.uk}}</ref> {| class="wikitable mw-collapsible" !Areas ![[Kirklees Borough Council|Kirklees]] Wards !Former Constituency |- |[[Batley]] |Batley East, and Batley West |[[Batley and Spen (UK Parliament constituency)|Batley and Spen]] |- |[[Dewsbury]] |Dewsbury East, Dewsbury South, and Dewsbury West |[[Dewsbury (UK Parliament constituency)|Dewsbury]] |- |[[Flockton]] / [[Grange Moor]] |Kirkburton (minority) |Dewsbury (plus 30 voters from [[Huddersfield (UK Parliament constituency)|Huddersfield]]) |}
