'''Doncaster East and the Isle of Axholme''' is a [[List of UK Parliament constituencies|constituency]] of the [[House of Commons of the United Kingdom|House of Commons]] in the [[Parliament of the United Kingdom|UK Parliament]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=The 2023 Review of Parliamentary Constituency Boundaries in England – Volume one: Report – Yorkshire and the Humber {{!}} Boundary Commission for England |url=https://boundarycommissionforengland.independent.gov.uk/2023-review/2023-review-volume-one-report/the-2023-review-of-parliamentary-constituency-boundaries-in-england-volume-one-report-yorkshire-and-the-humber/ |access-date=2023-07-25 |website=boundarycommissionforengland.independent.gov.uk}}</ref> Further to the completion of the [[2023 Periodic Review of Westminster constituencies]], it will first be contested at the [[2024 United Kingdom general election|2024 general election]].

The seat covers eastern areas of [[Doncaster]] in [[South Yorkshire]] and the [[Isle of Axholme]] in [[Lincolnshire]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Mower |first=Shannon |date=30 Jun 2023 |title=‘Doncaster East and the Isle of Axholme’ constituency to replace Don Valley at next election |url=https://www.doncasterfreepress.co.uk/news/people/doncaster-east-and-the-isle-of-axholme-constituency-to-replace-don-valley-at-next-election-4203947 |website=Doncaster Free Press}}</ref>

== Boundaries ==
The constituency composed of the following (as they existed on 1 December 2020):

* The City of Doncaster wards of: Finningley; Hatfield; Rossington & Bawtry; Thorne & Moorends.
* District of North Lincolnshire wards of Axholme Central; Axholme North; Axholme South.<ref name=":02">{{Cite web |title=The Parliamentary Constituencies Order 2023 |url=https://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2023/1230/schedules/made |at=Schedule 1 Part 9 Yorkshire and the Humber region}}</ref>

It comprises the following:<ref>{{Cite web |title=New Seat Details – Doncaster East and the Isle of Axholme |url=https://www.electoralcalculus.co.uk/fcgi-bin/calcwork23.py?seat=Doncaster%20East%20and%20the%20Isle%20of%20Axholme |access-date=2023-07-29 |website=www.electoralcalculus.co.uk}}</ref>

In the [[City of Doncaster]]:

* [[Finningley]], [[Hatfield, South Yorkshire|Hatfield]], [[Rossington]], [[Bawtry]] and [[Thorne, South Yorkshire|Thorne]] from [[Don Valley (UK Parliament constituency)|Don Valley]] (abolished)
* [[Moorends]] from [[Doncaster North (UK Parliament constituency)|Doncaster North]]

In [[North Lincolnshire]]:

* The [[Isle of Axholme]] from [[Brigg and Goole (UK Parliament constituency)|Brigg and Goole]] (abolished)

