{{Short description|Parliamentary constituency in the United Kingdom, 2024 onwards}} {{Infobox UK constituency |name=Pontefract, Castleford and Knottingley |parliament = uk |image = {{maplink|frame=yes|frame-align=center|plain=yes|raw={{Wikipedia:Map data/Pontefract, Castleford and Knottingley (UK Parliament constituency)}}|frame-height=200|frame-width=250}} |caption = Boundaries since 2024 |image2 = [[File:Yorkshire and the Humber - Pontefract, Castleford and Knottingley constituency.svg|215px|alt=Map of constituency]] |caption 2= Boundary of Pontefract, Castleford and Knottingley in Yorkshire and the Humber |year = 2024 |abolished = |previous = [[Normanton, Pontefract and Castleford (UK Parliament constituency)|Normanton, Pontefract and Castleford]] |next = |elects_howmany = One |electorate = |type = County |region = England |county = [[West Yorkshire]] |towns = {{ubl|[[Pontefract]]|[[Castleford]]|[[Knottingley]]}} |mp = [[Yvette Cooper]] |party = [[Labour Party (UK)|Labour]] }} '''Pontefract, Castleford and Knottingley''' is a proposed [[List of UK Parliament constituencies|constituency]] of the [[House of Commons of the United Kingdom|House of Commons]] in the [[Parliament of the United Kingdom|UK Parliament]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=The 2023 Review of Parliamentary Constituency Boundaries in England – Volume one: Report – Yorkshire and the Humber {{!}} Boundary Commission for England |url=https://boundarycommissionforengland.independent.gov.uk/2023-review/2023-review-volume-one-report/the-2023-review-of-parliamentary-constituency-boundaries-in-england-volume-one-report-yorkshire-and-the-humber/ |access-date=2023-07-25 |website=boundarycommissionforengland.independent.gov.uk}}</ref> Further to the completion of the [[2023 Periodic Review of Westminster constituencies]], it will first be contested at the [[2024 United Kingdom general election|2024 general election]]. [[Yvette Cooper]] is the incumbent MP for all parts of this new seat.
== Boundaries == The constituency composed of the following wards of the [[City of Wakefield]] (as they existed on 1 December 2020):<ref>{{Cite web |title=New Seat Details - Pontefract, Castleford and Knottingley |url=https://www.electoralcalculus.co.uk/fcgi-bin/calcwork23.py?seat=Pontefract,%20Castleford%20and%20Knottingley |access-date=2023-07-29 |website=www.electoralcalculus.co.uk}}</ref>
* [[Airedale and Ferry Fryston]] * [[Altofts and Whitwood]] * [[Castleford Central and Glasshoughton]] * [[Knottingley (electoral ward)|Knottingley]] * [[Pontefract North]] * [[Pontefract South]]<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |title=The Parliamentary Constituencies Order 2023 |url=https://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2023/1230/schedules/made |at=Schedule 1 Part 9 Yorkshire and the Humber region}}</ref> ''It will comprise the current [[Normanton, Pontefract and Castleford (UK Parliament constituency)|Normanton, Pontefract and Castleford]] seat excluding the [[Normanton (electoral ward)|Normanton]] ward, which includes the town of [[Normanton, West Yorkshire|Normanton]] and the civil parishes of [[Warmfield cum Heath]] and [[Kirkthorpe]].''
