Laila Cunningham was originally selected as the [[Conservative Party (UK)|Conservative]] candidate for the seat, but withdrew shortly before the nominations deadline. As the party did not field a replacement, it is the only seat in [[Great Britain]], aside from the Speaker's seat of [[Chorley (UK Parliament constituency)|Chorley]], in which no Conservative candidate was nominated.<ref>{{cite news|url = https://www.telegraph.co.uk/news/2024/06/07/tory-withdrawal-rotherham-labour-cunningham-election-reform/|title = Conservatives fail to field candidate in Rotherham|last = Gutterdige|first = Nick|date = 7 June 2024|newspaper = [[The Daily Telegraph]]|accessdate = 7 June 2024|url-access = subscription}}</ref>
